      ":question/id": "33917a1f-7610-5fed-a2a3-0addbb191168",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator?\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $\\frac{13\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{5\\pi}{6}$.*",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $\\frac{13\\pi}{12}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{5\\pi}{6}$.\n\nRecall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x+y)=\\sin x\\cos y+\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(\\frac{13\\pi}{12}\\right) &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{-\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
