      ":question/worked-solution": "Write the angle as a sum or difference of special angles: $\\frac{11\\pi}{12}=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\n\nRecall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y)=\\sin x\\cos y-\\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed unit-circle values, multiply, and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sin\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right) &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ &=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
